preserves maintained by Mages. But if they were to be a Kith, I'd probably want to have the legs just because it would seem to be such a big part of their identity.<br /> <br /> I wish I had a copy of the CoD Changing Breeds book, as I recall it having centaurs in it, and I'm sort of curious how they handled the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T11:41:43-07:00","id":1225381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1225340-opinions-on-centaurs?p=1225378#post1225378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always sort of saw them as more of a Bygone race than a Changeling one (sort of like unicorns and dragons), that now sadly exist primarily only in the Dreaming or hidden mystic preserves maintained by Mages. But if they were to be a Kith, I'd probably want to have the legs just because it would seem to be such a big part of their identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plenty of attempts as making a Dragon Kith out there.. and Mokole and... well Nymphs both work as inanimae and various spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wish I had a copy of the CoD Changing Breeds book, as I recall it having centaurs in it, and I'm sort of curious how they handled the issue. </div> </div> </div>The Horse changing Breed had Centaur as one of their forms. Since the COD book was meant to be a build yourown beast setup it could do things like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-06T11:58:24-07:00","id":1225388,"title":"","content":"We\u2019re I to write up a centaur kith for CtD, I\u2019d just make it a feature that mortals mistake them as being horseback or riding a motorcycle, etc when they use the Birthrights that reflect their physical mien (unless they call upon the Wyrd to reveal their true form of course).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"",